.TH SYNTH 1
.SH NAME
synth \- algorithmic scale-walk melody composer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dreammachines/synth
.RI [ nnotes
.RI [ seed
.RI [ major | minor | penta ]]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Synth
is a work-alike of the audio chapter of Nelson's
.IR "Computer Lib/Dream Machines" :
the computer as an instrument generating music, not merely reproducing
it. It composes a melody with a scale-constrained random walk \(em
every step lands on an in-scale degree by construction, small steps
heavily favoured, an occasional bigger leap or repeated note, the
whole walk clamped to a two-octave range \(em renders the result into
.IR tone (2)'s
own TempleOS-style Play() notation, and hands it off to
.B tone->play()
to actually perform through
.BR /dev/audio .
.PP
.I Nnotes
defaults to 24,
.I seed
to 1 (a given seed always composes the same tune \(em the actual
thing checkable about this without listening to it), and the scale
defaults to
.B penta
(major pentatonic: C D E G A), the interval choice generative-music
sketches lean on because it has no strongly dissonant step in it at
all;
.B major
and
.B minor
(natural, rendered with sharps uniformly) are also available.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/dreammachines/synth.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR tone (2)
